    "body": "> docker commands in WSL2, but the docker containers normally run on the same Docker as Windows run containers, so you don't connect to them through WSL2, or do you?\n\nDocker commands in WSL2 use the Docker *inside* WSL2, not Windows Docker. So you *do* connect to them through WSL2.\n\nThat said, [WSL Containers](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/wsl-container?tabs=csharp) were introduced recently which would probably also work really well for these use-cases (or would work for my needs at least) so if that's easier to integrate 🤷🏼‍♂️.",
