    "updated_at": "2026-08-09T15:23:38Z",
    "body": "I know you can run it in other configurations, but the one I'm using right now is Docker Desktop with WSL integration. When I open a WSL2 project with VS Code and then open the devcontainer of the project, it creates them as containers in my Docker Desktop that bind the ext4 directory tree from WSL2 (instead of using 9p to get the NTFS directory).\n\nI'm not familiar with WSL Containers, thank you, I'll check it up.",
