    "body": "[I've set up a workaround for this](https://thorgalle.me/notes/using-zed-with-remote-dev-containers-through-an-ssh-wrapper) using Zed's support for Remote Development through SSH. The idea is to route the commands Zed sends over SSH into your dev container using SSH configuration on the remote host. Zed then thinks it's talking to an (aliased) SSH host, but it's actually talking to your dev container. The linked post explains the details. I've used this approach myself successfully for some weeks now.\n\nTo be upfront about the limitations:\n- You need to use the [devcontainers/cli](https://github.com/devcontainers/cli) on the host to create or start containers. This workaround only helps Zed attach to running dev containers.\n- You need admin access to the SSH configuration on the remote host and client, and a new, dedicated key pair.\n- An SFTP server needs to be installed in the dev container (in most cases).\n- Only tested with docker so far, not with podman\n\nI hope this can help some people watching this thread while we're waiting for native support 🤞",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
